From c5b476b18fd15e045dc084e92047afb02de005d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hs-ye <ye.hansang@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:32:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] Fix silent mic: sink-backed virtual microphone

The Audio/Source pw_stream is never scheduled on this system: the node
reports `running`, its link is active and the format negotiates, but its
process callback is never invoked, so consumers only ever receive silence.

Play PCM into a private null sink and republish its monitor with
module-remap-source, keeping the historical device name. A sink always has
a driver, so the graph actually runs. An in-process playback stream
segfaulted inside libpipewire during setup, so PCM is fed via pw-cat.

Also:
- treat audio arriving outside Streaming as an implicit stream start; a
  reconnect can leave the remote streaming without re-sending AUDIO_START
- add a DC blocker: decoded frames carried a large positive bias that the
  20 dB gain turned into clipping
---
